{
  "_comment": "DLQ record contract, shared byte for byte by every implementation. One record per failed source message: the key and value are the source message key and value, unchanged. The headers are the source headers in their order, minus every header whose name starts with \"dk-\", then the dk- headers in header_order. A dk- header whose value is absent (null, or an empty delivered_sinks) is not written; 0 is a value. dk-error is the error text with URL credentials redacted, then cut to error_cut_bytes bytes at a UTF-8 character boundary. dk-delivered-sinks is the sorted list joined with \",\". dk-failed-at is the RFC 3339 UTC text with six fraction digits and \"Z\". Encoding of bytes in this file: a JSON string is its UTF-8 bytes, {\"base64\": \"...\"} is the decoded bytes, null is no value (a null key, or a header with a null value). failed_at in an input is the text the header carries. execute_error_text_cases pin the error text of the execute stage: \"exit code <n>: \" when the task has an exit code, then stderr, else the exception text, else the failure kind; expected_dk_error is that text after the cut.",
  "record_version": "1",
  "header_order": [
    "dk-record-version",
    "dk-stage",
    "dk-error",
    "dk-sink",
    "dk-task-id",
    "dk-attempts",
    "dk-delivered-sinks",
    "dk-source-topic",
    "dk-source-partition",
    "dk-source-offset",
    "dk-source-timestamp",
    "dk-request-id",
    "dk-worker",
    "dk-instance",
    "dk-failed-at"
  ],
  "error_cut_bytes": 2000,
